        "original_id": "3ba7e876-8a6a-5a5b-9a1b-cb6cf160862e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Nikolaas Tinbergen, Konrad Lorenz, William Homan Thorpe, Karl von Frisch, Patrick Bateson, Robert Hinde\n- Roles: biologist, ornithologist, zoologist, ethologist\n- Awards: Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine\n- Topics: animal behaviour, behavioural biology\n\nFacts:\n- Konrad Lorenz was born on 7 November 1903 and died on 27 February 1989.\n- Nikolaas Tinbergen was born on 15 April 1907 and died on 21 December 1988.\n- Konrad Lorenz was an Austrian zoologist, ethologist, and ornithologist.\n- Nikolaas Tinbergen was a Dutch biologist and ornithologist.\n- Nikolaas Tinbergen shared the 1973 Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine with Karl von Frisch and Konrad Lorenz.\n- The 1973 Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine recognized discoveries concerning the organisation and elicitation of individual and social behaviour patterns in animals.\n- William Homan Thorpe, Nikolaas Tinbergen, Patrick Bateson, and Robert Hinde contributed to the growth and acceptance of behavioural biology in Great Britain.",
